From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:17:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DRMPRIME: fall back to GL when the plane refuses a video

When the kernel refuses the video plane as set up, for example a 256x110
video scaled to 3840x1638 on RK3568, whose VOP2 planes scale up by at
most eight, every frame's request fails its test commit and the bridge
sends the same one again with the next frame, so the video is never
shown.

Test each new size and position of the video plane on its own with a
TEST_ONLY commit and leave the plane alone when the kernel refuses it.
CRendererDRMPRIME then reports a configuration change and its Create()
declines pictures of the refused size, so that CRendererDRMPRIMEGLES
renders the video. That renderer takes DRM PRIME pictures with either
renderer setting, as it is the fallback of the direct one.

Since commit 41c6d07329be ("GBM: move video plane teardown from renderer
dtor to FlipPage"), the bridge of a replaced CRendererDRMPRIME is torn
down at the next FlipPage(), and that teardown expects the GUI and the
video plane apart. CRendererDRMPRIMEGLES sets up its output in
SetVideoOutput() before that FlipPage(), where the single output plane
becomes the video plane, so SetVideoOutput() disables and releases a
bridge left behind first, through the same teardown as FlipPage().

Fixes: 87a783978517 ("VideoPlayer: add DRM PRIME renderer")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
